{title: Amazing Grace}
{artist: Edwin Othello Excell; John Newton; John P. Rees; William W. Walker}
{key: G}
{ccli: 22025}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Amazing [G7]Grace, how [C]sweet the [G]sound,
That [G]saved a [G7]wretch like [D]me.
I [G]once was [G7]lost, but [C]now im [G]found,
Was [Em]blind, but [D]now I [G]see.

{comment: Verse 2}
Twas [G]grace that [G7]taught my [C]heart to [G]fear,
And [G]grace my [G7]fears [D]relieved.
How [G]precious [G7]did that [C]grace [G]appear,
The [Em]hour I [D]first [G]believed.

{comment: Verse 3}
Through [G]many [G7]dangers, [C]toils and [G]snares
I [G]have [G7]already [D]come.
T'was [G]Grace that [G7]brought us [C]safe thus [D]far
And [Em]Grace will [D]lead us [G]home.

{comment: Verse 4}
When [G]we've been [G7]there ten [C]thousand [G]years,
Bright [G]shining [G7]as the [D]sun
we've [G]no less [G7]days to [C]sing god's [D]praise
Than [Em]when we [D]first [G]begun.
